# Quicken personal data — only sanitized fixtures under Samples/quicken/fixtures/
# are committed. Top-level QIF/CSV exports contain real account names and
# transaction history and must stay local.
Samples/quicken/*
!Samples/quicken/fixtures/
!Samples/quicken/fixtures/**

# Anything dropped into Samples/Downloads/ is treated as sensitive — service
# account JSON keys, credential exports, etc. Never commit these.
Samples/Downloads/

# Real bank-data exports from fintable / moneysheets / similar tools.
# Contain real account UUIDs, IBANs, balances, transactions — keep local.
Samples/Fintable/
Samples/Moneysheets/

# Custodian statements (Fidelity INVESTMENT REPORT PDFs). Carry full name, home
# address, account numbers and complete per-security holdings — strictly more
# sensitive than the QIF exports above. `parse-fidelity-statement.js` reads them
# from here; nothing is committed, and there are deliberately NO pinned fixtures
# for the parser because a scrubbed one would still be a real statement layout
# wrapped around real balances.
Samples/Fidelity/

# Filed tax returns (CR082 / FBAR work). The most sensitive class in this repo:
# a return carries SSNs for the filer AND spouse, dates of birth, home address,
# dependants, and the FinCEN 114 account numbers — i.e. every field the CR082
# security note (secrets-inventory: names and locations, NEVER values) exists to
# keep out of documents. Nothing under here is ever committed, and there are
# deliberately no fixtures: a redacted return is still a real return's layout
# wrapped around real figures. Extracted FBAR data belongs in Postgres, not here.
Samples/Tax/

